SEQUENCE:2026091401
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T205000
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast B (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Thu. Dec. 10 · Call 7:30 PM · 8:10 PM–8:50 PM · Robinson
  Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 7:30 PM: dancers must 
 be checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 7:15 PM. BA: Call Tim
 e is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minut
 es before Call Time.\nACT II Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair 
 and Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHA
 NGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal 
 are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/
 1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP
  for Coffee: Arabian Coffee — Costume (you provide): Flesh-tone Camiso
 le Leotard\, No tights\; Shoes: Flesh-tone Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Full S
 tage Makeup - Mascara Only OK\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\nFull Stage Mak
 eup Instruction Sheet:\n•  Apply foundation and powder matching ski
 ntone\n•  Light skin tone eye shadow over entire eye\n•  Dark 
 brown eye shadow over crease\n•  Medium brown eye shadow blended ov
 er brown\n•  Black fake eyelashes (note: apply mascara to own lashe
 s before application of fake lashes)\n•  Apply eyeliner after lashe
 s dry\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer do
 esn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n•  Brown or tan on co
 ntour cheekbones\, hairline\n•  Use a brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to
  darken the eyebrows\n•  Red or Dark Red Lipstick\nDancers of Color
  may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care G
 uidelines:\n•  Handle costume pieces with care while changing to pr
 event damage to delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansa
 s in the event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter h
 ow significant\n•  Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor
 \, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sittin
 g on the floor while in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\
 , clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage
  make-up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smud
 ging make-up on costume during its removal\n•  Refrain from the use
  of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear any ga
 rment not assigned to cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume food
  or beverage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do 
 not remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theat
 er\n•  Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs fo
 llowing their use\n•  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\
 n•  Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ war
 drobe policies\n•  Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or
  anything that may damage or stain costumes.
