 nd the BA portal are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.co
 m/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUM
 E / HAIR / MAKEUP for Coffee: Arabian Coffee — Costume (you provide): 
 Flesh-tone Camisole Leotard\, No tights\; Shoes: Flesh-tone Ballet Shoes
 \; Makeup: Full Stage Makeup - Mascara Only OK\; Hair: High Bun\, No Par
 t\nFull Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n•  Apply foundation and po
 wder matching skintone\n•  Light skin tone eye shadow over entire e
 ye\n•  Dark brown eye shadow over crease\n•  Medium brown eye 
 shadow blended over brown\n•  Black fake eyelashes (note: apply mas
 cara to own lashes before application of fake lashes)\n•  Apply eye
 liner after lashes dry\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply pl
 enty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n•  B
 rown or tan on contour cheekbones\, hairline\n•  Use a brow pencil 
 (or eyeshadow) to darken the eyebrows\n•  Red or Dark Red Lipstick\
 nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes
 .\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Handle costume pieces with care whi
 le changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly noti
 fy Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the point of discov
 ery\, no matter how significant\n•  Never throw costumes or accesso
 ries on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n•  Re
 frain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n•  Do not attempt
  to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n•  
 Never apply stage make-up while in costume and shall take great care to 
 refrain from smudging make-up on costume during its removal\n•  Ref
 rain from the use of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n•  
 Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n•  Do not handl
 e or consume food or beverage while in costume\, with the exception of w
 ater\n•  Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms 
 or from the theater\n•  Remove all bobby pins used to secure head p
 ieces and wigs following their use\n•  Return all headpieces to the
 ir assigned bags\n•  Comply fully with any and all updates to Balle
 t Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n•  Do not pack markers\, paints\, 
 colored drinks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
